High-Level (FAANG / Oracle / Microsoft)
44. What is the difference between abstraction and abstract class?
Abstraction is an OOP concept: hiding implementation details and exposing only essential behavior.
Abstract class is a Java language feature used to help achieve abstraction.
45. Why would Spring Framework use abstract classes?

Spring uses abstract classes to provide partial implementations so subclasses don't have to implement every method.

Example:

abstract class AbstractController {
    // common logic
}

The framework provides reusable behavior, and developers only implement what's specific to their use case.

